      "description": "Watch Inter Miami vs Columbus Crew highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The clash between Inter Miami CF and Columbus Crew in MLS promised to be a showcase of attacking football and tactical intrigue. On August 2, 2026 , fans were treated to a rollercoaster encounter where momentum shifted repeatedly between two determined sides. A Dramatic First Half Exchange Inter Miami seized the initiative early in the match, finding their breakthrough in the 16th minute. Yannick Bright provided a clinical assist for Luis Suarez , who finished with aplomb to ignite the home crowd. However, the lead was erased in unfortunate circumstances for the hosts when Casemiro inadvertently sent the ball into his own net in the 34th minute, gifting Columbus Crew an equalizer. Just as it seemed the teams would head into the break level, Inter Miami struck again deep into first-half stoppage time. In the 45+5th minute, Luis Suarez turned provider, setting up Noah Allen for a crucial goal that restored the lead. The atmosphere was electric as the referee blew for halftime shortly after, with Miami holding a narrow advantage. Messi's Impact and the Late Leveler The second half saw the introduction of Lionel Messi , who replaced Daniel Pinter in the 53rd minute to a roar of approval. While Miami looked to control the tempo, the game became increasingly physical. Sekou Tidiany Bangoura and Casemiro both saw yellow cards as the intensity peaked. Columbus Crew ’s persistence eventually paid off in the 84th minute. Substitute Brais Mendez , who had replaced Daniel Gazdag earlier, found the target to make it 2-2. Despite late drama that saw goalkeeper Patrick Schulte cautioned during five minutes of added time, neither side could find a winner. The final whistle at 90+8' confirmed a hard-fought draw in what was a classic Major League Soccer battle."
