      "description": "Watch Columbus Crew vs FC Cincinnati highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. Two Major League Soccer rivals squared off in a highly anticipated clash that promised intensity and tactical intrigue. On July 26, 2026 , the stage was set for a battle where every decision and every moment of brilliance would prove crucial. Early Dominance for the Hosts The match began with an electric energy as Columbus Crew looked to establish their authority from the opening whistle. In just the 9th minute, the deadlock was broken when Kevin Denkey found the back of the net following a precise setup by Evander Ferreira . This early strike gave the home side a wave of confidence, and they continued to test the FC Cincinnati defense with high-tempo play that left the visitors struggling to find their rhythm. Expanding the Lead Before the Break As the first half progressed, Columbus Crew remained relentless in their pursuit of goals. In the 41st minute, Jamal Thiare doubled the advantage after being picked out by Dylan Chambost . The situation went from bad to worse for FC Cincinnati deep into first-half stoppage time when the referee pointed to the penalty spot. In the 45+6th minute, Daniel Gazdag stepped up and coolly converted the penalty, ensuring his side went into the interval with a commanding cushion. Discipline and Late Drama The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as both managers looked to the bench, with the likes of Malte Amundsen and Chase Adams entering for the hosts. While FC Cincinnati tried to fight their way back into the contest, their frustrations boiled over in the closing stages. Matt Miazga had already seen yellow in the 66th minute, but the real flashpoint occurred in the 90+3rd minute. Gerardo Valenzuela was shown a yellow card followed immediately by a red card, sparking heavy protests from his teammates. With a man down and time running out, the visitors could not find a response during the ten minutes of added time."
